Z||000004||mrfiero||03-01-2000||06:24 PM||||ALWAYS keep the car running (idling) when you wash the engine compartment!  That way you'll know when you get too close to the electrical stuff (it'll start to sputter).<P>As for the white stuff, that is probably the dielectric grease (or the remnants thereof) used to prevent the wires from seizing to the plugs.||||reg||3
Z||000005||Uaana||03-04-2000||08:17 AM||||Please let me know if these purchases correct your hesitation problem.<P>To give you a partial anwser.. With just the new plug wires in I can allready tell the difference. (the old ones were really shot)<BR>I'm still planning on the coil anyways, not that I expect much more but with just the wires replaced most of the hesitation is gone.||||reg||1
